# Render Environment Variable Safety

## The wipe problem

`PUT /v1/services/{id}/env-vars` **replaces ALL env vars** with the body you send.
If your body omits variables that are currently set, those variables are silently deleted.
This has caused two production outages in this project (ALLOWED_ORIGINS wiped → dashboard 500).

## Required: always use render_env_safe.py

Never write raw `PUT /env-vars` requests in scripts or one-off Python snippets.

```bash
# ✅ Safe — merges into existing, preserves everything else
python3 scripts/render_env_safe.py srv-xxxx KEY=value KEY2=value2

# ✅ Safe — dry run shows what would change
python3 scripts/render_env_safe.py srv-xxxx --dry-run KEY=value
```

```python
# ✅ Safe — import and use in Python scripts
from scripts.render_env_safe import render_env_upsert
render_env_upsert('srv-xxxx', {'KEY': 'value', 'KEY2': 'value2'})

# Delete a key safely (set value to None)
render_env_upsert('srv-xxxx', {'STALE_KEY': None})
```

```python
# ❌ NEVER do this — wipes everything not in payload
payload = [{'key': 'MY_KEY', 'value': 'val'}]
requests.put(f'https://api.render.com/v1/services/{svc}/env-vars', json=payload)
```

