## Critical vars that must always be present on auraflux-api

If any of these are missing, the service boots but the dashboard breaks silently:
- `ALLOWED_ORIGINS` — CORS whitelist. Missing = all browser requests return 500.
- `CLERK_SECRET_KEY` — auth. Missing = all authenticated routes 401.
- `STRIPE_SECRET_KEY` — Stripe init at load time. Missing = server crashes on startup.
- `REDIS_URL` — queue. Missing = BullMQ crashes, no job processing.
- `DATABASE_URL` — Postgres. Missing = all job queries fail.

## Hardening status (as of June 2026)

### ✅ Render Secret Files — DONE
Critical secrets (Clerk, Stripe, DB, Redis, all API keys) are stored in an encrypted-at-rest
Secret File (`.secrets.env`) on `auraflux-api`. `server.js` loads it via dotenv at startup from
`/etc/secrets/.secrets.env`. The file is never visible in build logs or Render dashboard UI.

Secrets in the file: `CLERK_SECRET_KEY`, `STRIPE_SECRET_KEY`, `STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET`,
`DATABASE_URL`, `REDIS_URL`, `R2_ACCESS_KEY_ID`, `R2_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY`, `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY`,
`OPENAI_API_KEY`, `GEMINI_API_KEY`, `HEYGEN_API_KEY`, `RUNPOD_API_KEY`, `SMTP_PASS`, `GITHUB_API_TOKEN`.

To update a secret: use `render_env_safe.py` for env vars, OR use the
`PUT /v1/services/{svc_id}/secret-files` endpoint with the full merged file content.

